    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Terrace',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Terrace is a two-deck solitaire for one player. Shuffle two decks; 11 cards face-up reserve, 8 foundation piles, 9 tableau piles. Deal 3 to three tableaus, choose one for first foundation (only that rank to foundations). Build foundations up in alternating colours (A between K and 2); tableaus down in alternating colours. Reserve: only top card to foundations. Empty tableau filled from stock or discard. Goal: move all 104 cards to foundations.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Family: Terrace. Categories: Thinker's, Rewarding, Two-Deck, Large. Also known as Queen of Italy; origin inferred from alias. No detailed timeline documented in primary source.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'One player. Terrace is a solitaire (two-deck patience) for a single player.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two standard 52-card decks shuffled together (104 cards).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two decks, table space for reserve, eight foundations, nine tableaus, stock and discard.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Shuffle both decks. Lay 11 cards face-up in a row as the reserve. Below, eight empty foundation piles and nine empty tableau piles. Deal three cards from stock face-up, one to each of three tableaus. Choose one of these three to move to the first foundation; only cards of that rank may start other empty foundations. Deal seven more cards from stock, one onto each remaining empty tableau. Remaining cards form the stock (face-up, squared). Discard pile starts empty.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
